Fix the Eclipse 2026-09 (4.41) startup crash: DevStyle's CSS-engine weaver
hardcodes a superclass that no longer exists.

DevStyle's startup bundle registers IgnoreCSSClassPatch, an ASM class weaver
for org.eclipse.e4.ui.css.swt.engine.CSSSWTEngineImpl. The applyStyles(Object,
boolean) override it injects ends with an INVOKESPECIAL of the superclass
method, with the owner spelled out as AbstractCSSSWTEngineImpl. Eclipse 4.41
collapsed that hierarchy (CSSSWTEngineImpl now extends CSSEngineImpl directly
and AbstractCSSSWTEngineImpl is gone), so loading the woven class fails with
NoClassDefFoundError inside ThemeEngineManager.getCSSSWTEngine — before any
workbench window exists, hence the bare "An error has occurred" dialog
(upstream report: github.com/Shadows-of-Fire/revstyle issue #7).
Use the woven ClassNode's own superName as the owner: INVOKESPECIAL resolves
the inherited method through the actual superclass on every release, so the
patched weaver is behavior-neutral on 4.40 and earlier.

Target: com.genuitec.eclipse.startup 2025.2.0.202509301431
Context source: VineFlower 1.12.0 output (--folder --use-lvt-names=1) of the
bundle jar. Details: docs/css-weaver-superclass.md

--- a/com.genuitec.eclipse.startup/src/com/genuitec/eclipse/startup/patches/IgnoreCSSClassPatch.java
+++ b/com.genuitec.eclipse.startup/src/com/genuitec/eclipse/startup/patches/IgnoreCSSClassPatch.java
@@ -102,7 +102,11 @@
